From c1af3108466248d42f63bccc1d015ce44fab5c79 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 16:31:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] presence: report the active players, and revoke the leaked
 1.6.5 token
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two independent fixes that happen to touch the same server.

PRESENCE. The account server keeps ONE presence table for the whole network (the
Switch friend list, the website and every other game read it), and this server
never wrote to it: a player in this game was OFFLINE to all of their friends for
as long as they played. presence.go reports the active PIDs every 30 s — the
implementation splatoon-2 has been running — with the shared internal key,
without which the account server drops the report. The title id comes from
nextendo-account's own game table so the friend list names the right game.

REVOCATION. The token leaked by the 1.6.5-win release was revoked in the account
server and in some game servers; the map here was EMPTY, so that credential
still played online — and, through the 'one place at a time' gate, kept the real
owner offline. revoked.go also loads NEXTENDO_REVOKED_TOKENS(_FILE) so the next
revocation is one deployment rather than nine source edits that drift.
---
 main.go         |  12 +++++
 presence.go     | 118 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 revoked.go      |  87 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 revoked_test.go |  55 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 272 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 presence.go
 create mode 100644 revoked.go
 create mode 100644 revoked_test.go

